# Gina package transition (product memory)

## Direction

- Primordial build: **Gina / Asistente**. **Agents sidebar card retired** — specialists temporarily listed under Assistance (see `assistant-single-card-roadmap.mdc`).
- Intel tools that stay (**Launch Radar**, **Forecast**, **Event calendar**, Market Hype, etc.) remain in **their panel only** — not as a multi-agent package.

## Credits → capacity model

- Current Pro UX: **~200 monthly credits**.
- Target package: assistant may feel **unlimited**, but delivery is capped by **provider capacity** (calls + time window / TPS), e.g. Groq-style **5 000 calls / ~6 h TPS** — that defines the sold package, not a pure credit counter.
- Measure package viability from **Recent Calls** + quota meters (provider included / window / overage), not by moving the ledger to Sheets.

## While building

- Do not redesign billing UX around hours until that package brief is scheduled.
- Do not remove Launch Radar / Forecast panels when retiring Agents.
- Prefer instrumenting provider windows (anchor, reset, time left) over inventing new credit types.
